==English==

===Etymology===
Latin [[salutatio]] “a greeting, a wishing health to,” from [[saluto]] “wish one’s health, greet,” from [[salus]] “well-being.” Cf. the Latin greeting ''[[salvere|salve]]'' “be well.”

===Noun===
'''salutation'''
{{wikipedia}}
#A [[greeting]], [[salute]], or [[address]]; a [[hello]].
#The act of greeting.
#The title in your name, such as Mr, Mrs, Ms., Dr. or Rev..

